+// The screen is cut in LIGHT_GRID_W x LIGHT_GRID_H tiles; each tile holds one bit per light for the nearest
+// 32 omni lights (x) and the nearest 32 spot lights (y) whose bounding sphere touches the tile.
+// The view depth is cut in LIGHT_GRID_Z slices of equal length up to the farthest light; each slice holds the
+// same kind of bits for the lights whose depth range touches it. A pixel's lights = tile bits AND slice bits.
+#define LIGHT_GRID_W 24
+#define LIGHT_GRID_H 12
+#define LIGHT_GRID_Z 64
